													<p><a href="/page/prospective-applicationprocedure.html" class="link-003 icon left prev">CJP Application Procedure </a></p><p><img src="https://ciec.kwansei.ac.jp/upload/S27_Website%20Banner.png" alt="S27 Website Banner" class="responsive"></p>

<p class="a-center"><a href="#h3-001" class="link-003 icon right down anchor">Program Overview</a><a href="#h3-005" class="link-003 icon right down anchor">About the Study Tracks</a> <a href="#h3-002" class="link-003 icon right down anchor">Application Procedure</a> <a href="#h3-004" class="link-003 icon right down anchor">Enquiry</a> <a href="#h3-003" class="link-003 icon right down anchor">About Accommodations</a></p>

<h3 id="h3-001">Program Overview</h3>
<p>You can find an overview of the program in the latest Contemporary Japan Program (CJP) Brochure. 
<br>In the brochure, you will find details about the two study tracks, available courses and much more.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://ciec.kwansei.ac.jp/study/exchange/outline/pdf/CJP%20Brochure%20(2026-2027)%20(PDF).pdf" target="_blank" class="btn yellow icon left next white"><span style="color:#111 !important; font-weight:600;">Latest CJP Brochure</span>
</a>
<h3 id="h3-005">About the Study Tracks</h3>
<p>After reviewing the CJP Brochure above for an overview of the program, use the guide below to help choose the best study track for your goals. 
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://kwansei.box.com/s/f6soo8iktu4k8j4nog01spuidfinmuvv" target="_blank" class="btn yellow icon left next white"><span style="color:#111 !important; font-weight:600;">How To Choose Your Study Track</a></p>
<div style="text-align: center;">
  <ul style="display: inline-block; text-align: left; padding-left: 1em;" class="icon-kome">
    <li style="padding-left: 0.5em;">Understand the difference between the two tracks (JLT & MJT)</li>
    <li style="padding-left: 0.5em;">Take a self-check quiz to reflect on your goals</li>
    <li style="padding-left: 0.5em;">See sample course registration patterns</li>
    <li style="padding-left: 0.5em;">Get advice based on learning style and class preferences</li>
  </ul>
</div>
<h3 id="h3-002">Application Procedure</h3>
<dl class="step">
<dt><strong>01</strong></dt>
<dd>
<h5>Online Nomination</h5>
<p>Applicants must be nominated by their home/sending institutions prior to the nomination deadline. <br>Nominations received after the deadline may not be accepted.<br>A new nomination link will be sent to partner institutions every semester when applications open. If your institution has not received the new link, please have them email the KGU Incoming Team (<a href="incoming[a]kwansei[d]ac[d]jp" class="icon left mail"></a>) as soon as possible.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<dl class="step">
<dt><strong>02</strong></dt>
<dd>
<h5>Gathering all Application Documents</h5>
<p>A complete application may contain up to 14 documents. Please access the below website to find details about the application documents and their format.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://app.jotform.com/kwansei-gakuin-university/s27-kgu-intake" target="_blank" class="btn orange icon left next white"><span style="color:#111 !important; font-weight:600;">2027 Spring Semester Intake - Application Website</span></a></p>
<ul class="icon-kome"><li>All documents must be written in English or Japanese. If the document is written in another language, it must be accompanied by an English or Japanese translation.</li><li>Hand written forms (except the "Certificate of Health") are NOT accepted.</li><li>Use the designated format when specified.</li></ul>
</dd>
</dl>
<dl class="step">
<dt><strong>03</strong></dt>
<dd>
<h5>Submission of Required Documents</h5>
<p>Before submitting the soft copies to your home university's international office so they can send your full application to us, please make sure you followed all the directions.</p>
<ul class="icon-kome"><li>All files available must be submitted in PDF format except the digital ID photo that can be submitted as a JPG file.</li><li>If your professor followed the dedicated procedure, document number 05 has already been uploaded to our platform and <strong>does not need to be submitted again</strong>. You will receive a confirmation email once the submission is completed.</li><li>Please label your files 'Application Number - Document Number Form Name.pdf', eg. 'S27-999 - 01 Application Form.pdf'</li></ul>
<p>Once you have checked all your application documents, <strong>send them to your home university's exchange coordinator for review</strong> and submission ahead of the deadline. Your home university's exchange coordinator <strong>has received a submission link </strong>to use for this purpose.</p>
<h5>⚠️Application Deadline: November 15</strong> ⚠️</h5>
</dd>
</dl>
<h3 id="h3-004">Enquiry</h3>
<p>If you have any questions about the application procedure, the schedule or any other questions about the program, please use the below Enquiry Form.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://form.jotform.com/222637761952463" target="_blank" class="btn blue icon left next white"><span style="color:#e0e0e0 !important; font-weight:600;">Exchange Program - Enquiry Form</span></a></p>

<p><br />
<h3 id="h3-003">Regarding Accommodations</h3><br />
<p>All nominated students are eligible to apply for KGU-arranged accommodation. While we cannot at this time guarantee that they will receive a housing placement, we assure you that the KGU Residence Center will make every effort to accommodate as many students as possible. <br>The KGU Residence Center will be in touch by early November with details about the Accommodation Application/Request process but in the meantime, you can find a quick overview of the accommodation options we offer on the page below.</p><br />
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="/study/exchange/studentlife/accommodation.html" target="_blank" class="btn blue icon left next white"><span style="color:#e0e0e0 !important; font-weight:600;">About Accommodations</span></a></p></p>

<p>Any student who would rather arrange for their own accommodation or who would not be successful in obtaining a KGU-arranged accommodation as a result of the housing application process can review the information available on the above page for guidance on how to find a suitable self-arranged accommodation in our area and a few recommendations.</p>

<p><a href="/page/prospective-applicationprocedure.html" class="link-003 icon left prev">CJP Application Procedure </a></p>
													
